---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="max-w-4xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-12 text-gray-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-gray-600">
      At Medeligo Cancer Research, we respect the privacy of clinicians,
      scientists, and informed patients who rely on our oncology-focused search
      engine. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect
      information when you interact with the platform. By using the site, you
      agree to the practices described below.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our platform is designed to minimize the personal data we gather. We
        collect:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Usage Metrics:</strong> Anonymous or pseudonymous analytics data
          such as page views, query patterns, device characteristics, and approximate
          geographic region.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Search Activity:</strong> The keywords you submit, saved libraries,
          and related interactions used to deliver relevant medical literature.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical Logs:</strong> System logs that help us monitor performance,
          diagnose errors, and secure the service.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We do not intentionally collect sensitive identifiers such as patient
        data, social security numbers, or payment details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">2. How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>
        We use collected information to operate and enhance our search
        capabilities, surface more relevant oncology research, prevent abuse,
        and maintain reliable performance. Aggregated insights guide product
        improvements that align with the needs of the medical research
        community.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">3. Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Medeligo relies on analytics services to understand platform engagement.
        These providers process usage data strictly on our behalf and under
        confidentiality agreements. We do not share user information with any
        third parties beyond these analytics partners, and the data is used
        solely to improve platform experience and stability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">4. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
      <p>
        We may use cookies or similar technologies to remember session
        preferences, maintain saved article libraries, and measure service
        performance. You can adjust browser settings to limit or disable
        cookies; however, doing so may impact certain features.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">5. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain analytics records and search metadata only for as long as
        necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this policy. When data is
        no longer required, we anonymize or securely delete it in accordance
        with industry best practices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Safeguarding research activity is important to us. We employ
        administrative, technical, and organizational measures to protect
        against unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure of collected
        data. Despite these efforts, no security controls are infallible, and
        users should exercise caution when sharing sensitive information online.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">7. Your Choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may opt to clear browser storage, adjust cookie preferences, or
        cease using the platform at any time. For assistance with data requests
        or questions about your information, contact us using the details below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">8. International Users</h2>
      <p>
        Medeligo operates from the United States. If you access the platform
        from other regions, you consent to the transfer and processing of
        information in accordance with U.S. laws, which may differ from those in
        your jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">9. Children&apos;s Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are not intended for individuals under 13 years of age. We
        do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you
        believe a child has provided us with data, please contact us so we can
        remove it promptly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">10. Updates to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our operations
        or legal requirements. Updated versions will include a revised effective
        date, and material changes will be highlighted on the site. Continued
        use after updates indicates your acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">11. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or to submit a data request,
        please email
        <a
          class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700"
          href="mailto:privacy@medeligo.com"
        >
          privacy@medeligo.com
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Medeligo does not provide medical advice or warranty the accuracy of
        external research. You are responsible for validating findings with
        qualified healthcare professionals.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
